From 06a1e9973a8ad0719265c2d556569fdfac3a1485 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bradent27-sketch <304192343+bradent27-sketch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:21:46 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Retire v2_xtd_missing_prior_share (the plain missing-prior
 fix; v2_xtd_missing_prior_overall ships)

2026-11-02: a player absent from last season's zone usage (a rookie) had his real zone share blended with a fake 0 prior at weight
K / (games + K), so a rookie's expected TDs ran 0.2x in week 2 and about 0.43x after three games (rookie RB rushing TDs per carry
0.009 against 0.027 for veterans). The plain fix gives such a player NO prior (his current share stands alone); it failed weeks 1-2
(START-ALL +0.019, REJECT) because a 3-game zone share is noisy. The overall variant, which shrinks it toward his overall share of
the team's opportunities, passed and ships. xtd_blended_rate loses the missing_prior_unknown option (a team with no opportunities yet
still falls back to the no-prior behaviour); the test now exercises the overall variant against the no-fix baseline.
Restore with git revert of this commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
